WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.136
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.405
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.907
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:10.143 line:0%
Well, guys, it was a big day
here in New York,

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:14.314 line:0%
as Andrew Cuomo announced that
he is resigning as governor.

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:17.250 line:0%
During his remarks, he said it
was best that he step aside.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.253
And then every woman in the room
took two steps aside.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:22.788
During his announcement,

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:26.292
Cuomo said that
he's stepping down in 14 days.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.460
I'm sorry, but is this really a

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.730
two-week-notice
type of situation?

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.064
It's gonna be tough for Cuomo.

00:00:32.064 --> 00:00:34.400
With a track record like this,
his only future is either

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.068
president or
Supreme Court justice.

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:37.737
So, you know...

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:40.673
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:41.907
Cuomo's replacement will be

00:00:41.907 --> 00:00:44.377
Lieutenant Governor
Kathy Hochul.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.411
And this is -- Yeah.
[ Crowd cheering ]

00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:46.712
This is strange.

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:49.015
Right after she was announced as
New York's next governor,

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:51.317
CNN offered a prime-time show
to her sister.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.019
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:56.589
What a day.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.224
The news definitely
can't get any worse

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.126
for powerful guys named Andrew.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:02.728 line:0%
-Prince Andrew
facing a new lawsuit filed by

00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:05.932 line:0%
Jeffrey Epstein accuser
Virginia Roberts Giuffre.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:09.268
-Okay, maybe it can get worse.

00:01:09.268 --> 00:01:11.137
Today, the queen called
Harry and Meghan and was like,

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:14.374
"Can I crash with you
for a while?"

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:15.708
It's been such a tough year,

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:16.976
the queen now answers
the phone like,

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.545
"Oh, good Lord, what now?"

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:21.647
When his lawyer said he'll never
get another job again,

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:24.050
Prince Andrew was like,
"Another what?

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.087
Job?"

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.689
How about we shift gears
to some positive news, huh?

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:32.792 line:0%
Today, the Senate passed
President Biden's

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:37.296 line:0%
$1.2 trillion infrastructure
bill with bipartisan support.

00:01:37.296 --> 00:01:38.498 line:0%
That's --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.967
That's good news.
That's positive.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.505
That's right --
a trillion dollars to fix

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:48.340
our roads, bridges,
and airports.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:49.842
So after they finish LaGuardia,

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:53.513
that will leave us
with about 40 bucks.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:56.448
It's amazing we can pass a
$1 trillion infrastructure bill,

00:01:56.448 --> 00:02:00.185
yet we can't find the new host
for "Jeopardy!"

00:02:00.185 --> 00:02:04.523 line:0%
Speaking of crazy things,
Florida governor Ron DeSantis

00:02:04.523 --> 00:02:07.093 line:0%
is threatening to withhold pay
from any school officials

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:10.163 line:0%
who require masks.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.898
I'm nervous about DeSantis.

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.599
I mean, right now people in
Florida are like,

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:15.100
"When can Cuomo start?"

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.535
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:19.505
That's not good, you know?

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:21.874
As employers around the country
urge their workers

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:24.977
to get vaccinated,
the owner of an eyewear store

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:26.946
ran into a strange concern
from one employee.

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.214
Watch this.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.716 line:0%
-An optical-business owner
says he can't convince

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:32.818 line:0%
all of his employees
to be vaccinated.

00:02:32.818 --> 00:02:35.554 line:0%
One employee said she was
concerned because she thought

00:02:35.554 --> 00:02:38.224 line:0%
a vaccine had caused
the characters in the film

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:41.828 line:0%
"I Am Legend"
to turn into zombies.

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:45.398
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:47.433
-So I'm guessing the
requirements to get a job

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:51.036
at that store
are not that demanding.

00:02:51.036 --> 00:02:52.838
Seriously, vaccine or not,
you might want to

00:02:52.838 --> 00:02:54.774
stop that woman
from coming into the office.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.242
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.543
Some entertainment news.

00:02:57.543 --> 00:03:00.513
Last night was the final episode
of "The Bachelorette."

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:01.747
We love that show. Yeah.

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:03.082
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:05.251
And one of the
big moments from the episode

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:09.255
was when the final contestant,
Blake, met Katie's Aunt Lindsey.

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.657
Take a look at how their
conversation went.

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:14.193
-So, what made you
want to go on this season

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:16.095
after you flunked
out of the last one?

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:18.064
-Yeah, flunked.
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:19.765
Yeah, I've been dumped twice.

00:03:19.765 --> 00:03:21.267
There was two Bachelorettes
that showed up.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.735
One left --
-And neither of them wanted you?

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:23.802
-I guess not.

00:03:23.802 --> 00:03:27.172
-Like,
you ultimately mean nothing.

00:03:27.172 --> 00:03:29.542
Like, hate to break it to you,
but, like,

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:33.145
you better be secure as [bleep]
coming into our family,

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:36.282
because at the end of the day,
you're here because

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.517
we want you here,
not because we need you here.

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:40.820
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.788
-It's nice when someone welcomes
you into the family

00:03:42.788 --> 00:03:46.425
by quoting Joe Pesci
in "Goodfellas."

00:03:46.425 --> 00:03:48.127
That's right -- the season
finale of "The Bachelorette"

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:52.064
was last night, and Katie and
Blake are officially engaged.

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:53.900
You know that show
can get pretty emotional,

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.200
so I thought we could help.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.236
Here's a clip from
the episode re-voiced

00:03:57.236 --> 00:04:00.306
with the least-emotional person
we know, Siri.

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:02.842
This is "Let's Get Siri-ous."

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.076
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:04.076 --> 00:04:06.111
-[ Whispering ]
"Let's Get Siri-ous."

00:04:06.111 --> 00:04:08.581
-[ Robotic voice ]
My entire day and evening

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.783
with Blake was truly perfect.

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.051
Yum. Yum.

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:14.053
And the fact that we could
open up the way we did

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.822
during the dinner, it really
changed our relationship.

00:04:16.822 --> 00:04:18.290
Last night was, I think,

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.159
everything I could have
hoped for.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:21.160
Me, too.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.661
Mwah.

00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:26.132
Mwah. Mwah.
Mwah.

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:27.767
Mwah.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.802
Mwah. I love you.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:31.170
Mwah.
Love you, too.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.439
Mwah. Bye. Bye.

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:34.607
Mwah, mwah, mwah.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:35.841
Alright.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.841 --> 00:04:37.577
"Mwah, mwah, mwah."

00:04:39.945 --> 00:04:42.315
That's right -- as I said,
it was a three-hour finale

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:43.683
of "The Bachelorette,"
and a lot of people

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:46.885
are talking about the
"After the Final Rose" special,

00:04:46.885 --> 00:04:48.387
when Katie -- You know what
I'm talking about?

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:50.857
Katie confronted her ex, Greg.

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:52.358
Yeah, but you don't have to
take my word for it,

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:54.126
because here to
re-enact this moment

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:57.529
with actual lines from the show
are Tariq and Questlove.

00:04:57.529 --> 00:04:58.631
Guys.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:04.903 --> 00:05:06.405
-Thanks, Jimmy.

00:05:06.405 --> 00:05:10.342
Tonight, I'll be playing Katie,
who is finally about to accuse

00:05:10.342 --> 00:05:13.946
her ex, Greg,
of lying about his intentions.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:15.380
-And I'll be playing Greg,

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:18.851
who is about to experience
Katie's full wrath.

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:21.353
-Great. Well, whenever
you guys are ready.

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:27.260
♪♪

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:30.663
-You're saying I'm not
"validating" you enough,

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:35.001
but it's like,
you got a First Impression Rose.

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:37.270
You got a first one-on-one.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:41.707
The second one-on-one,
every single group date.

00:05:41.707 --> 00:05:43.542
Oh, man, I feel like

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:46.245
you were never ready
for an engagement.

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:49.915
-I'm honestly so confused
as to why you would think that.

00:05:49.915 --> 00:05:53.018
Um, I wouldn't -- Wow!

00:05:53.018 --> 00:06:01.527
-You didn't even
bother to say goodbye.

00:06:03.128 --> 00:06:05.431
You say you love me,

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:08.367
but I don't think
you know what love is,

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:11.904
because that
was a time I needed...

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:14.674
I needed you the most...

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:20.246
and you ran away.

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:23.382
-Well, I understand that you
found what you're looking for.

00:06:23.382 --> 00:06:26.018
-Oh, absolutely!

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:28.888
I am very happy.

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:30.957
Oh, but -- but
that doesn't take away from

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:33.425
the anger
and the way you treated me --

00:06:33.425 --> 00:06:36.295
using me to get
the experience, the exposure,

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:41.067
dare I say, the acting practice
at my expense!

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:45.004
-[ Chuckles ]
The acting?

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:47.206
-I mean, it was pretty good.

00:06:47.206 --> 00:06:52.078
Until the end, when you kind of
F'd it up and ran away!

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:54.680
-Look,
I hate to break it to you,

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:59.018
but as much as I wish I was,
I'm not Meryl Streep.

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:01.287
-Oh, we know.

00:07:01.287 --> 00:07:02.355
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:02.355 --> 00:07:05.457
-Wow. Oh, my God!
That was unbelievable.

00:07:05.457 --> 00:07:07.593
That's Questlove and Tariq,
everyone.

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:09.395
That was actually unbelievable.

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:11.831
Oh, my -- Wow. Wow.

00:07:11.831 --> 00:07:14.500
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's very nice.

00:07:15.668 --> 00:07:17.536
Mm-hmm.

00:07:17.536 --> 00:07:20.572
Yeah, thank you.
Good to see you.

00:07:20.572 --> 00:07:22.374
Questlove and Tariq, everybody.
Yeah, there you go.

00:07:22.374 --> 00:07:25.744
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:25.744 --> 00:07:26.846
Well, get this.

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:29.047 line:0%
I read that Disney
just released the prices

00:07:29.047 --> 00:07:32.551 line:0%
for its new "Star Wars"
Galactic Starcruiser hotel,

00:07:32.551 --> 00:07:37.089 line:0%
and it can cost you up to $6,000
for a two-night stay.

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:38.757
While over at the Marriott,

00:07:38.757 --> 00:07:42.628
6 grand will get you
the entire Marriott.

00:07:42.628 --> 00:07:44.029
Yeah, 6 grand.

00:07:44.029 --> 00:07:46.599
Even worse, when you ask for
the "Star Wars" honeymoon suite,

00:07:46.599 --> 00:07:48.467
they say it's booked by
a brother and a sister.

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:50.503
[ Audience groans ]

00:07:52.605 --> 00:07:53.605
-Come on!

00:07:53.605 --> 00:07:56.909
-That's...
-Come on. Luke and Leia.

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:59.644
-Well, finally, I saw that
Pepsi and Boston Beer

00:07:59.644 --> 00:08:03.048
are teaming up to create
an alcoholic Mountain Dew drink

00:08:03.048 --> 00:08:04.783
called Hard Mountain Dew.

00:08:04.783 --> 00:08:05.818
Here's a photo.

00:08:05.818 --> 00:08:08.621
Yeah.

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:11.958
Meth is actually
a gateway drug to that.

00:08:16.828 --> 00:08:19.531
What's crazy is that half
of America refuses the vaccine

00:08:19.531 --> 00:08:22.468
but will have no problem
putting that into their body.

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:25.004
Can we see the cans again?

00:08:25.004 --> 00:08:28.274
They look like what a kid
draws to show his parents

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:30.476
what his nightmares are about.

00:08:30.476 --> 00:08:32.778
Hard Mountain Dew
is actually a lot healthier,

00:08:32.778 --> 00:08:34.079
because the
alcohol helps kill whatever

00:08:34.079 --> 00:08:35.214
is in normal Mountain Dew.

